WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:10.130
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-ninth of June. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:17.440
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, got you. Only just made it in, mind. Traffic on the ring road was absolutely crawling.</v>

00:00:18.519 --> 00:00:22.719
<v Callum Reid>Same. Ten minutes looking at the back of the same skip wagon.</v>

00:00:24.739 --> 00:00:31.039
<v Sarah Okafor>While we're on vehicles, whose new car is that in the car park? Very shiny for this place.</v>

00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:37.729
<v Aisha Begum>Mine. Give it a week, it'll be the same colour as everyone else's.</v>

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.899
<v Jamie Brennan>Factory grey. Comes free with the parking space.</v>

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:53.049
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. And the heating in the portakabin's still making it feel like November indoors, except backwards. Anyway, that's me moaning, not a job request.</v>

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:57.689
<v Hannah Price>I've got the window open and I'm still cooking.</v>

00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:02.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, quick round. Finished stuff first, then what actually needs agreeing.</v>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, tested the boiler safety valve yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:11.069 --> 00:01:13.870
<v Hannah Price>That's finished, then? Nothing outstanding from the test?</v>

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.980
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Finished, yeah. All fine. Just closing the loop.</v>

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:23.950
<v Jamie Brennan>And I signed off the inspection on the Compressed Air Dryer on Tuesday. That's already done as well.</v>

00:01:25.599 --> 00:01:28.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Last Tuesday, yeah? Not something booked for tomorrow.</v>

00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:33.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Last Tuesday, correct. Old news, just hadn't said it on here.</v>

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:39.790
<v Tomasz Nowak>I've already swapped the filter on the pick and place on two yesterday, as well.</v>

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.069
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, nights knew that had been done.</v>

00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:48.469
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good. Nothing else on that from me.</v>

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:57.890
<v Callum Reid>Couple of observations, then. Noticed the number two bearing was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:59.989 --> 00:02:02.790
<v Aisha Begum>Settled back to normal, or just stopped climbing?</v>

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:09.479
<v Callum Reid>Back to normal. Just passing on what we saw, not putting another job up.</v>

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.650
<v Callum Reid>Also saw the pressure on the HV switchboard dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:20.610
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, you clipped out. Came back without anyone doing anything?</v>

00:02:22.689 --> 00:02:25.139
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, on its own. Again, observation only.</v>

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:33.840
<v Olumide Adeyemi>My blocker hasn't changed. Still waiting on parts for the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.460
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, they're not here. No arrival to report, unfortunately.</v>

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:43.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, that stays blocked. Not dressing it up as something we can get done today.</v>

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.960
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll do a site visit at Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor this afternoon.</v>

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:54.330
<v Hannah Price>Right, I've got Sarah Okafor against that one, this afternoon.</v>

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:03.360
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I'll write up the near miss at the stretch wrapper first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:10.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz. That's holding production up so it needs doing first. First thing tomorrow, as you said.</v>

00:03:10.919 --> 00:03:14.770
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. I'll do that first thing tomorrow, ahead of anything else.</v>

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.250
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, the write-up's the bit we're held on. That needs to stay at the top.</v>

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:31.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you grease and check the bearings on the line 3 screw by Wednesday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:38.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take that. Grease and check the bearings on the line 3 screw by Wednesday.</v>

00:03:39.259 --> 00:03:44.159
<v Aisha Begum>Just—sorry, talking over you. That needs the downtime lined up with production, doesn't it?</v>

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:54.060
<v Sarah Okafor>It does. We need someone to schedule downtime for the line 3 screw with production tomorrow. Who can take the scheduling bit?</v>

00:03:55.449 --> 00:04:01.400
<v Callum Reid>I can't take ownership of that one. Don't put it against me just because you said production.</v>

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:10.430
<v Jamie Brennan>And I'm accepting the bearing work, not the downtime scheduling. Just so we're not assuming I've picked up both.</v>

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:18.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Scheduling downtime for the line 3 screw with production tomorrow is needed, but it's unowned. Nobody's taken it.</v>

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:23.779
<v Jamie Brennan>The bearing work is still mine, by Wednesday. I'm not dropping that.</v>

00:04:24.829 --> 00:04:28.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Not an emergency, but that Wednesday deadline doesn't slip.</v>

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:34.680
<v Hannah Price>There's also organising the toolbox talk for the team after lunch. That still needs someone.</v>

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:41.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, after lunch, whenever you get a chance. It's not a drop-everything one. Any takers for organising it?</v>

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:44.579
<v Hannah Price>I'm flagging it rather than volunteering, sorry.</v>

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.509
<v Callum Reid>I can't take that either, I'm afraid.</v>

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Toolbox talk organisation stays unassigned, then. Nobody against it.</v>

00:04:54.550 --> 00:05:01.550
<v Olumide Adeyemi>One more needing an owner: run a function test on the line 2 guard by the end of the week.</v>

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:08.319
<v Hannah Price>That's fairly important. By the end of the week, definitely, rather than letting it drift.</v>

00:05:08.829 --> 00:05:13.029
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah. I'm raising it, not saying I'll do it. Haven't taken ownership.</v>

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.009
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't commit to that one either.</v>

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:25.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Function test on the line 2 guard: fairly important, by the end of the week, still nobody owning it.</v>

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:39.500
<v Sarah Okafor>So the agreed owners are me for Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor this afternoon, Tomasz for the stretch wrapper near-miss write-up first thing tomorrow, and Jamie for the line 3 screw bearings by Wednesday.</v>

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:44.000
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep. Grease and check, both. Got it.</v>

00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:49.290
<v Tomasz Nowak>And mine is first thing tomorrow, first priority because it's holding production up. Clear.</v>

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:59.899
<v Hannah Price>I've kept the boiler safety valve, Compressed Air Dryer inspection and that filter swap in the completed bit. Not mixed into the new work.</v>

00:06:02.189 --> 00:06:08.139
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Correct. And the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller is still the parts blocker, not a fresh action.</v>

00:06:09.379 --> 00:06:13.930
<v Callum Reid>My two things were just observations too. Neither's me volunteering for another job.</v>

00:06:15.629 --> 00:06:30.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. The gaps are still downtime scheduling with production tomorrow, toolbox talk organisation after lunch whenever someone gets a chance, and the fairly important line 2 guard function test by the end of the week. All three unowned, not silently handed to anyone.</v>

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:35.079
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, that's clear. Better than everyone thinking someone else said yes.</v>

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Right, thanks everyone. I'll let you escape Teams.</v>
